[b]Room design and materials[/b]

Matched workshop views show the paving and furnishing changes. Fixed lifting equipment, sorting surfaces, manual trays and a trackless handcart replace the earlier rails.

[SPOILER=Workshop before and after]

[i]Prepared native render — Workshop before: the protected foundation.[/i]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/autismoyah-hub/project-gielinor-showcase/83e1b40d52b34bcbe50b5d9662f5a61a37bb2282/images/tower-map/08-workshop-before.png[/img]

[i]Prepared native render — Workshop after: fitted slate, machine pads and manual workstations; the old rails are removed.[/i]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/autismoyah-hub/project-gielinor-showcase/83e1b40d52b34bcbe50b5d9662f5a61a37bb2282/images/tower-map/09-workshop-after.png[/img]

[/SPOILER]

Live room captures show the sanctuary, preparation areas, waterworks and encounter chambers. Stone, brick and refractory floors distinguish their uses.

